l3.statement:
We assume:
• n is an odd integer [tc_1];
• There exists an integer k such that n = 2*k + 1 [l1];
• For the integer k from [l1], n^2 = 4*k^2 + 4*k + 1 [l2].
Therefore, we conclude:
• For the integer k from [l1], n^2 = 4*k*(k + 1) + 1 [l3].

