l5.statement:
We assume:
• (a_n) is an arithmetic sequence [tc_1];
• a₁ = 5 and a₃ = 11 [tc_2];
• There exists a common difference d such that a₃ = a₁ + 2d [l1];
• 11 = 5 + 2d [l2];
• 2d = 6 [l3];
• d = 3 [l4].
Therefore, we conclude:
• a₅ = a₁ + 4d [l5].

ts_1.statement:
We assume:
• (a_n) is an arithmetic sequence [tc_1];
• a₁ = 5 and a₃ = 11 [tc_2];
• For the arithmetic sequence (a_n), there exists a common difference d such that for all n, a_n = a₁ + (n-1)d [def_1];
• a₃ = a₁ + 2d [l1];
• 11 = 5 + 2d [l2];
• 2d = 6 [l3];
• d = 3 [l4];
• a₅ = a₁ + 4d [l5];
Therefore, we conclude:
• a₅ = 17 [ts_1].
